# Q. What is Dependency Injection & Its Types?

Dependency Injection means one object depends on another object.

Example:
If one class requires another class object to work, it is called dependency injection.

---

# Types of Dependency Injection
# Setter Injection (Setter Dependency Injection)

## Definition

Setter Injection (or Setter Dependency Injection) is a type of **Dependency Injection (DI)** in which Spring injects values into a bean using **setter methods**.

The Spring IOC Container creates the object and calls the setter methods automatically to inject the required values.

---

## Why Setter Injection?

Without Spring, values are assigned manually:

```java
Player p = new Player();
p.setId(1);
p.setName("Virat");
p.setRun(12000);
```

With Spring, the container automatically injects these values through XML configuration.

---

## Advantages of Setter Injection

1. Easy to implement.
2. Supports optional dependencies.
3. Values can be modified after object creation.
4. Improves readability.
5. Promotes Loose Coupling.
6. Easy maintenance and testing.

