        <property name="name"
                  value="Virat"/>

        <property name="run"
                  value="12000"/>

    </bean>

</beans>
```

---

## Theory of XML Tags

### `<bean>`

Used to create and manage objects in Spring Container.

```xml
<bean id="p"
      class="org.techhub.Player">
```

| Attribute | Description                |
| --------- | -------------------------- |
| id        | Unique bean identifier     |
| class     | Fully qualified class name |

---

### `<property>`

Used for Setter Injection.

```xml
<property name="id" value="1"/>
```

Spring internally calls:

```java
player.setId(1);
```

Similarly,

```xml
<property name="name" value="Virat"/>
```

calls

```java
player.setName("Virat");
```

and

```xml
<property name="run" value="12000"/>
```

calls

```java
player.setRun(12000);
```

