## Step 5: Create Client Application

### PlayerClientApplication.java

```java
package org.techhub;

import org.springframework.context.support.ClassPathXmlApplicationContext;

public class PlayerClientApplication {

    public static void main(String[] args) {

        ClassPathXmlApplicationContext context =
                new ClassPathXmlApplicationContext("player.xml");

        Player player =
                (Player) context.getBean("p");

        System.out.println(
                player.getId() + "\t" +
                player.getName() + "\t" +
                player.getRun());

        context.close();
    }
}
```

---

## Theory of Client Application

### ClassPathXmlApplicationContext

```java
ClassPathXmlApplicationContext context =
new ClassPathXmlApplicationContext("player.xml");
```

Purpose:

* Loads XML configuration file.
* Creates Spring Container.
* Creates all beans defined in XML.
* Injects dependencies automatically.

---

### getBean()

```java
Player player =
(Player) context.getBean("p");
```

Purpose:

Returns the bean object created by Spring.

Equivalent to:

```java
Player player = new Player();
```

but Spring creates and manages the object.

