# 2. Constructor Injection / Constructor Dependency Injection

Constructor Injection means **Spring container creates object using constructor and passes values through constructor arguments**.

---

## Example 1: Default Constructor

### Bean Class

```java
package org.techhub;

public class Test {

    public Test() {
        System.out.println("I am default constructor");
    }
}
```

---

## XML Configuration

```xml
<bean id="t" class="org.techhub.Test"/>
```

Spring automatically calls:

```java
new Test();
```

---

## Client Application

```java
package org.techhub;

import org.springframework.context.support.ClassPathXmlApplicationContext;

public class ConstructorInjectApplication {
    public static void main(String[] args) {

        ClassPathXmlApplicationContext context =
                new ClassPathXmlApplicationContext("player.xml");

        Test t = (Test) context.getBean("t");

        context.close();
    }
}
```

### Output

```java
I am default constructor
```

